  "summary": "Goggles, dreadfalls and platform boots: the rave future made flesh.",
  "description": "Cybergoth fused goth's darkness with rave's neon: UV-reactive mesh, PVC and doll-hair dreadfalls, gas-mask respirators, lab goggles, platform New Rocks, and cyberlox braids in acid green and hot pink — a costume engineered for strobe-lit warehouses playing aggrotech, EBM and happy hardcore. Born from late-1990s UK/German industrial club scenes (the \"graver\" portmanteau), the style spread through European festivals and US cyber clubs, dropped from mainstream view in the 2010s, and was resurrected by TikTok fashion cycles. Its visual logic: the body as techno-console — tubing, straps, screens, and neon filaments everywhere.",
  "culturalContext": "Cybergoth fused goth and rave into club-ready futurism: born in UK-German industrial scenes, the style defined millennial cyber fashion, faded with EDM's rise, and TikTok resurrected it — goggles, dreadfalls and platforms as Gen Z's discovered heritage.",
